dence", "Neuromuscular Junction Disorder: Lacks specific features like ptosis or fatigability"], "alarm_features": ["Recent 17-pound weight loss", "Chronic alcohol and tobacco use", "Hypertension (177/108 mmHg)", "History of diabetes"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Brachial Plexopathy", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.3296451735978635, "posterior": 0.3397015553267312, "danger": 0.3, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Burning/dull pain with subacute onset aligns with plexopathy presentation patterns, suggesting strong clinical support for this diagnosis."], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3", "B1.4"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.5, "interrupt_relevance": 0.4, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "anatomy"}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Cervical Spine Compression with Nerve Root Involvement", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.038, "danger": 0.5, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Positional stability weakly contradicts cervical spine compression hypothesis (B2), maintaining its existing exclusion."]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Neurodegenerative / Paraneoplastic Syndrome", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.033, "danger": 0.75, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Positional normalization reduces concern for paraneoplastic (B3/B1.2) but does not definitively exclude it without testing."]}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Metabolic/Endocrine Neuropathy", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.214, "danger": 0.4, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Atypical pain distribution weakens metabolic/endocrine (B4) but doesn't exclude it entirely due to multiple overlapping comorbidities."]}, "B5": {"id": "B5", "label": "Vascular (Non-Ischemic) Upper-Limb Compression Syndrome", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.079, "danger": 0.3, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B1.1": {"id": "B1.1", "label": "Traumatic Brachial Plexopathy (Injection Site Injury)", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.106, "danger": 0.2, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Physical exam absence weakly contradicts traumatic brachial plexopathy (B1.1), balancing against prior risk from anabolic steroid use."]}, "B1.2": {"id": "B1.2", "label": "Paraneoplastic Brachial Plexopathy (Possibly Lung Origin)", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.053, "danger": 0.75, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Positional normalization reduces concern for paraneoplastic (B3/B1.2) but does not definitively exclude it without testing."]}, "B1.3": {"id": "B1.3", "label": "Diabetic Brachial Plexopathy (Diabetic Amyotrophy Variant)", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.053, "danger": 0.15, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Burning pain in diabetic setting contradicts diabetic amyotrophy's typical painless presentation, reducing its likelihood."]}, "B1.4": {"id": "B1.4", "label": "Idiopathic / Other Non-Specific Inflammatory Causes", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.128, "danger": 0.1, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}}, "frontier": [], "other_mass": 0.0, "pending_results": [], "actions_taken": [{"t": 4, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the subacute progressive nature of the deficit and presence of constitutional symptoms (weight loss, smoking) provide sufficient context to consider paraneoplastic syndromes as possible despite …", "summary": "Constitutional features and subacute course moderately support paraneoplastic syndromes while weakening metabolic/endocrine and traumatic alternatives."}, {"t": 4, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Is the patient's diabetes mellitus a sufficient risk factor to justify prioritizing diabetic brachial plexopathy over other steroid-associated neuropathies?", "summary": "Diabetes confounds differential with both weak metabolic support and weak support for steroid-associated plexopathy."}, {"t": 4, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Could the combination of diabetes, hypertension, and chronic alcohol use account for a metabolic/endocrine neuropathy with focal upper-limb manifestations rather than symmetric involvement?", "summary": "Metabolic/endocrine (B4) modestly supported, vascular compression (B5) gains parallel support via comorbidities. No direct effect on B1.3."}, {"t": 4, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the physical exam showing no positional symptom changes and lack of paraneoplastic markers (e.g., humoral hypercalcemia) sufficiently rule out paraneoplastic brachial plexopathy as a dangerous d…", "summary": "Positional normalization reduces concern for paraneoplastic (B3/B1.2) but does not definitively exclude it without testing."}, {"t": 4, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the diabetes history and absence of pain in typical metabolic neuropathy locations (e.g., feet, lower limbs) argue against a metabolic cause despite the patient's constitutional symptoms?", "summary": "Atypical pain distribution weakens metabolic/endocrine (B4) but doesn't exclude it entirely due to multiple overlapping comorbidities."}, {"t": 4, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the presence of localized burning pain argue against a generalized metabolic/endocrine process as the primary diagnostic explanation?", "summary": "Localized pain patterns are compatible with either metabolic/endocrine or focal inflammatory/infectious causes."}], "differential_history": [{"top": [["B1", 0.364], ["B4", 0.164], ["B1.1", 0.145]]}, {"top": [["B1", 0.33], ["B4", 0.238], ["B1.1", 0.118]]}, {"top": [["B1", 0.34], ["B4", 0.214], ["B1.4", 0.128]]}], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": false, "reason": "", "required_actions": []}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": false, "termination_type": "continue", "reason": "Leading branch (B1) posterior (0.3397) remains below 0.75 confirmation threshold. Dangerous paraneoplastic alternatives (B1.2, B3) with danger ≥0.75 exist but posteriors <0.10. Frontier contains unresolved sub-branches (B1.1-B1.4) requiring discriminators like MRI, CK levels, and paraneoplastic serology. Tree depth (3) has not been fully reached as root remains actionable with independent investigations."}, "turn_budget_used": 4, "estimated_remaining_value": 0.5, "max_turn_budget": 5, "latest_action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "diagnosis_readiness_score": 0.21396443220423964, "benchmark_output_ready": false, "static_question": "Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?", "static_options": [{"id": "A", "description": "Apical lung tumor"}, {"id": "B", "description": "Brachial plexopathy"}, {"id": "C", "description": "Cerebral infarction"}, {"id": "D", "description": "Scalenus anticus syndrome"}, {"id": "E", "description": "Subclavian steal syndrome"}], "seen_evidence_ids": [], "seen_evidence_phenotypes": "{'brachial plexopathy', 'Decreased cervical spine mobility', 'Brachial plexus neuropathy', 'Cervical spine instability', 'Spinal instability', 'Abnormality of the brachial nerve plexus', 'Burning sensation of skin', 'burning sensation', 'Decreased cervical spine flexion due to contractures of posterior cervical muscles'}", "mode_policy": {"benchmark_purity": true, "allow_external_knowledge": true}, "answer_option_mapping": {}, "tool_use_log": [], "root_revision_needed": false, "max_tree_depth": 3, "reasoning_ledger": {"anchor": {"hypothesis": "B1", "t": 0, "posterior_at_anchor": 0.488}, "leader": {"branch_id": "B4", "label": "Metabolic/Endocrine Neuropathy", "posterior": 0.214, "leading_since_t": 0, "n_revisions": 0}, "leader_evidence": {"confirming": 5, "disconfirming": 2, "last_disconfirming_digest": "Atypical pain distribution weakens metabolic/endocrine (B4) but doesn't exclude it entirely due to multiple overlapping…"}, "action_intents": [{"t": 4, "intent": "refute"}, {"t": 4, "intent": "confirm"}, {"t": 4, "intent": "confirm"}, {"t": 4, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 4, "intent": "refute"}, {"t": 4, "intent": "broaden"}], "considered_alternatives": ["B1.4", "B1.1", "B5"]}, "discriminator_hints": "[Knowledge Layer: coverage=57%, source=both]\n\nNeurodegenerative / Paraneoplastic Syndrome vs Traumatic Brachial Plexopathy (Injection Site Injury):\n  Favours first:  2-3 toe syndactyly, abdominal obesity, abnormal cardiac septum morphology, abnormal cardiac ventricular function, abnormal cerebral white matter morphology\n  Favours second: deformity of the arm or hand, difficulty moving the shoulder, arm, hand, or fingers, diminished arm reflexes, electric shock-like sensation, intense pain\n\nNeurodegenerative / Paraneoplastic Syndrome vs Paraneoplastic Brachial Plexopathy (Possibly Lung Origin):\n  Favours first:  2-3 toe syndactyly, abdominal obesity, abnormal cardiac septum morphology, abnormal cardiac ventricular function, abnormal cerebral white matter morphology\n  Favours second: deformity of the arm or hand, difficulty moving the shoulder, arm, hand, or fingers, diminished arm reflexes, electric shock-like sensation, intense pain\n\nNeurodegenerative / Paraneoplastic Syndrome vs Diabetic Brachial Plexopathy (Diabetic Amyotrophy Variant):\n  Favours first:  2-3 toe syndactyly, abdominal obesity, abnormal cardiac septum morphology, abnormal cardiac ventricular function, abnormal cerebral white matter morphology\n  Favours second: deformity of the arm or hand, difficulty moving the shoulder, arm, hand, or fingers, diminished arm reflexes, electric shock-like sensation, intense pain\n\nRelated to Neurodegenerative / Paraneoplastic Syndrome: humoral hypercalcemia of malignancy, oncogenic osteomalacia, paraneoplastic neurologic syndrome\n\n[Indirect reasoning chains (PrimeKG 2-hop):]\